A(r"""\documentclass[10pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=2cm]{geometry}\usepackage{booktabs,amsmath,graphicx}\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\usepackage{mathptmx}
\title{Supplementary Material\\\large Are Hybrid Ensembles Explained as Faithfully as the Single Model They Replace?}\date{}
\begin{document}\maketitle
All numbers below are generated by scripts in the code repository from the saved per-fold outputs. HE = hybrid ensemble; S* = internally selected single model; SV/ST = soft-voting/stacking ensembles of all five components.

\section*{S1. NDF definition details and validation}
NDF is computed as in Eq.~(1) of the paper with $K=\min(5,\#\{j:s\phi_j>0\})$, 50 deletion-background rows disjoint from the 50 SHAP-background rows, and 20 random orderings. Ties in signed attribution are broken by the lower feature index. NDF is undefined (and the patient excluded) if $K=0$ or $G\le10^{-12}$; the analysis gate is $G\ge0.05$ for both models. When $d\le K$ the $k=d$ term equals zero because deleting all features gives $D=1$ for every ordering. Before any real-data analysis the implementation passed known-answer tests: (K1) for additive models with known contributions, NDF of the true attribution matches its known value for $d\in\{5,10,13,30\}$ and random attributions give NDF $\approx0$; (K3) a correlated redundant feature is handled as specified; (K4) for a model with an interaction, SHAP scores above random attributions; (K5) a constant model is excluded. Further tests showed that a ranking by the smallest positive contributions scores below the true ranking, that ties are resolved deterministically, and that SHAP scores above random attributions for a probability-scale (logistic-link) model. (Test K2 of the protocol concerns the LIME conversion used only in a secondary analysis not reported in this paper.) SHAP additivity held to $10^{-14}$ and exact versus permutation SHAP agreed on small $d$.
""")
# S2 exclusions
A(r"\section*{S2. Exclusions, prediction gaps and absolute NDF (primary analysis, 25 folds $\times$ 20 patients)}")
A(r"\resizebox{\textwidth}{!}{\begin{tabular}{lrrrrrrrr}\toprule Dataset & Sampled & $G{<}0.05$ HE & $G{<}0.05$ S* & Included & Median $G$ HE & Median $G$ S* & Median NDF HE & Median NDF S*\\\midrule")
